FIX CartContext.jsx: replace the two competing useEffects with a lazy useState initializer. Recommended patch:

```jsx
const [items, setItems] = useState(() => {
  try {
    const stored = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
    return stored ? JSON.parse(stored) : [];
  } catch { return []; }
});

useEffect(() => {
  localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(items));
}, [items]);
```

Remove the first useEffect entirely — the lazy initializer reads localStorage synchronously before the first render, preventing the write-effect from ever seeing (and persisting) an empty `[]`.
